{
  "_comment": "Links to the server's own things (`<server>/m/<message_id>` M12b, `/c/` canvases, `/p/` pages, `/e/` events, `/d/` drive items, `/eq/` equipment), as every client recognises them in a body (desktop permalink.ts parseLink, iOS Permalink.swift, Android Permalink.kt). Only the server signed in to: its host (any case) and port (the default one may be written out or not) and its path; http and https both (2026-11-05: a link the server or a proxy wrote with the other scheme opened in the browser). Then the kind's path and a UUID (any case; the result is lower case), ending there or with `/`, `?` or `#` (what follows is ignored). Anything else (another server, another port, another kind, letters after the id) is not one and stays an ordinary link. Splitting a link from the text around it is the tokenizer's (inline-format.json). `kind`: m, c, p, e, d or eq; `id`: the id, or null when `url` is not such a link.",
